# The disk-usage view: what is taking up space, read straight from the search index.
#
# A harness run is unelevated, so MftVolumeIndexer.Open() fails soft on every volume and no
# dir_size_cache rows exist. That means this script can only photograph the *unknown* states —
# which is the coverage worth having here, since those are exactly the ones that regress into
# rendering zeros. What a populated view looks like is settled by the Core tests.

tree .
refresh

# Files come from the enumeration, so their sizes are real even with nothing indexed. Folders have
# no cached total, so they must read "Not measured" — never "0 B".
dialog disk-usage 01-unindexed

theme light-plus
dialog disk-usage 02-unindexed-light
theme dark-plus

# Drilling must not move anything. Clicking a rectangle reloads the view, and three things used to
# come and go with it — the progress bar, the "never been measured" footnote, and the banner — so
# the whole dialog shifted on every click. The progress bar and footnote now sit in containers that
# reserve their space, and the banner is docked at the bottom, where appearing cannot push the rest
# down (its height depends on its wording, so no fixed slot could hold it).
#
# These two are the same view over folders with different contents, one with subfolders and one
# without. Every fixed part must land on the same row in both: the headers, the map, the top of the
# list, the footnote and the banner. Put any of those three back in the flow and they separate.
dialog disk-usage 03-drill-before
go Documents
settle 300
dialog disk-usage 04-drill-after

# Nothing here may have tried to put another program's window on screen.
assert-not-launched
state
